for young people to have opportunities  we need to help them develop and people  talk about leadership but the first most  important thing about leadership is  understanding yourself your own  strengths maybe your own weaknesses as  well the things that you prefer and the  things that you find difficult and I  think what all of the young people on  the course find out is a lot more about  themselves which then it helps them to  go and lead other people and did you  draw on your own personal experience in  thinking that I can contribute something  to this yeah I think when you are in a  position where you're leading national  football team thankfully we've had good  results so people pay a little bit more  attention maybe to the way that you lead  and maybe there's a perception that you  have to be a certain character to be a  leader or to be in charge when actually  that personality can take all different  sorts of forms so you don't have to be  one type one personality type to be able  to lead other people successfully and  can you draw do draw in your involvement  in what happens in sport in football  what's happened to you with England you  can draw on that yeah I think it's  important when you're working with young  people that they recognize not only that  it's it's possible to succeed but that  before the success there's a lot of hard  learning and there's a lot of difficult  times and a lot of failures along the  way and I think it's fine to be open  about those things because that's part  of improvement and I think when you're  young you're working all of those things  out in your life you don't know maybe  necessarily exactly what you want to do  and you assume that everybody that's  older and appears successful on the  outside that life's been a breeze for  them and generally speaking all the  successful people I've ever met that  hasn't been the case  and because leadership is about how you  deal with those not failures but when  things don't go according to plan  I mean you've you with England  incredible success do you kind of brace  yourself for when the results are not  quite so good I mean do you do you sort  of look ahead and think how am I gonna  deal with that well I've had fair amount  of failure as well with so I'm pretty  well adapted to what that might be and  you you know that for every success  there will be difficult times but as a  leader you've got to take the rest of  the group through those difficult times  and keep them on track keep them focused  on the vision ahead and lead them  through those difficult spells they're  the biggest challenges for leaders that  people lose confidence in the plan if  you're if you're losing matches or if  there's difficult moments but there are  lots of things you could do when it  comes to sort of charities or helping  organizations what is a what is it about  this that you think that makes it  something where you can really  contribute and what are you going to be  doing yeah so this is I've worked with  the Prince's Trust for over 10 years  anyway so I have a good association and  a good understanding of the areas of of  their work I think it's so important to  invest in young people that is it's  obvious but they are the future of our  country and the more that we can develop  leaders and the more that we can give  young people confidence and then they  can go out and an opportunity then we're  affecting everything that happens in our  country so I'm in a position where  because of the role I mean I think I can  make a difference and I'm also working  with young people of this age every day  of my working life so and just finally  on this what would be your key message  then to maybe a young person who doesn't  feel confident even to apply for a you  know to come on a program like this what  would be your message to them yeah that  I think everybody in the world has  insecurities everybody and very often  that inhibits us from doing what might  be possible and really going for things  so sometimes the most difficult thing is  to pick up the phone and enroll in a  course  or to approach somebody to go on a  course and if you can make that step  then I think the experience of coming  and taking part in that leadership  journey will give them great skills for  the rest of their lives  all right let's talk briefly about  football I mean it's been the most  extraordinary 48 hours can you quite  believe what you witnessed with these  two wins by Liverpool and Tottenham well  I was at Manchester City on Monday so I  thought that was a incredible twist in  itself I was an Enfield on Tuesday so  left there thinking I'd seen one of the  most things I mean I've been in football  30 years one of the most incredible  nights I can remember for it then to be  backed up by Tottenham on Wednesday was  phenomenal I mean huge credit to both  managers in different circumstances  they've achieved incredible seasons and  from an England perspective brilliant  for all of our players that they're  having these experiences in big matches  where they're having to play under  pressure and they've come out  successfully is it good for England  though because you've got this issue now  haven't you it lands you in a bit of  trouble with the dates the Champions  League final on June the 1st you've got  the game semi-final of the National  League on the six so how much of a  headache is that for you then well it's  mate it's making things more complicated  that's for sure because reality is we  all get seven or eight of those players  three days before our semi finals so you  have great ideas as a manager of  planning things and working with the  team and in truth we'll have half of our  squad that won't be with us until three  days before so more complicated but  brilliant for for the players and  long-term for England we need them in  those matches and our job as their staff  is to adapt to those changes and make  sure that we're still prepared for the  semi-final with Holland so who's gonna  win a Champions League well thanks a  tricky one lately it is really difficult  because I think Liverpool have won the  matches between the two this year  but I've been the Champions League  matches I've been at this year I was in  Paris when Manchester United won which I  went there not thinking that was going  to happen I went to Anfield not thinking  that was going to happen it was saw  Spurs win against Manchester City which  certainly you know two minutes from the  end didn't look like it was going to  happen so it's been a remarkable year in  that competition and anything is  possible and luckily I don't care  actually as long as the English players  come through play well and stay fit then  I'm happy yeah  and just finally the Women's World Cup I  mean you know you've had a great World  Cup just recently last year what is your  message to them well they're ready you  know they're very they've got a nice  blend of some experienced players who've  been two World Cups before quite a few  of them have over a hundred caps you  know they were doing this before us they  were in a semi final four years ago so  and they've got some good young players  coming through as well so hugely  exciting summer for them we're all  supportive of what they're going to do  and I've my only advice would be to  enjoy it in the way that we did
 

